From 533abf443fbe9b1b3c1d91b51009652b9eb42ad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:33:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/23] convert : --outtype fp8_e4m3 writes native F8_E4M3
 GGUFs (M5)

- gguf-py: GGMLQuantizationType.F8_E4M3 = 43, GGML_QUANT_SIZES (128, 132),
  LlamaFileType.MOSTLY_F8_E4M3 = 42; quantize() passes packed blocks through.
- llama.h: LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_F8_E4M3 = 42 (same integer as gguf-py so the
  GGUF file type round-trips); ftype name + type->ftype guess mapping in
  llama-model-loader.cpp.
- conversion/base.py: _generate_fp8_tensors() reblocks weight +
  weight_scale_inv pairs into block_f8_e4m3 rows (NVFP4-style, before
  dequant_model), runs when ftype == MOSTLY_F8_E4M3; non-fp8 tensors default
  to BF16; E5M2 rejected; warns when no fp8 weights found; GUESSED heuristic
  detects float8_e4m3fn; index discovery falls back to any
  *.safetensors.index.json weight map (nonstandard part naming).
- conversion/qwen.py: transform_fp8_weight hook applies the V-head reorder to
  fp8 weight + scale grid in 128-row/col units.
- convert_hf_to_gguf.py: --outtype fp8_e4m3 choice (replaces --preserve-fp8).
- D3 gate extended to the plain GGUF path in llama_model_load (fp8 tensors +
  no fp8 device -> clear error, same as the safetensors path).
- safetensors loader writes general.file_type = 42 for fp8 models.

Verified: GGUF blocks byte-identical to source, 20-token parity exact vs the
safetensors path and bf16, PPL 8.715 (GGUF) == 8.716 (safetensors) vs 8.602
(bf16), gen 73-75 t/s, MTP 101 t/s, llama-server batched OK, CPU-only build
rejects with the fp8-device error.

